          "ARC-REV-01": {
            "evidence": [
              {
                "file": "src/Lending.Transition/Accounts.fs",
                "line": 19,
                "quote": "let totalOwed (library: Library) ="
              },
              {
                "file": "src/Lending.Application/Views.fs",
                "line": 337,
                "quote": "Owed = money (Accounts.totalOwed library) }"
              },
              {
                "file": "src/Lending.Application/UseCases.fs",
                "line": 175,
                "quote": "if ports.Archive.Exists path then"
              }
            ],
            "rationale": "The one new domain rule, the total all members owe (fines less payments), is defined in Tier 2 as Accounts.totalOwed. It is built on the existing Accounts.owed, and Tier 3 Views only calls it and formats the result. The summary is plain counts of collections (members, books, copies, loans; the tests show returned loans drop out of Loans) and the number of holds, which counts as projection. The no-overwrite check in UseCases.backup and the whole-state replacement in restore are rules about storing backups, not lending rules: no legal state or transition is decided in Tier 3/4. The CLI only sends commands to use cases and renders the views.",
            "score": 2
          },
          "ARC-REV-02": {
            "evidence": [
              {
                "file": "src/Lending.Application/Ports.fs",
                "line": 25,
                "quote": "Exists: string -> bool"
              },
              {
                "file": "src/Lending.Host/Persistence/JsonFileStore.fs",
                "line": 20,
                "quote": "Exists = fun path -> File.Exists path || Directory.Exists path"
              },
              {
                "file": "src/Lending.Host/Cli/CommandLine.fs",
                "line": 194,
                "quote": "| Ok [ \"backup\"; path ] -> UseCases.backup ports path |> render showBackup"
              }
            ],
            "rationale": "The new existence check is a new field on the existing Tier 3 Archive port, implemented by the Tier 4 persistence adapter. Backup, restore and backup-info reach files only through ports.Archive and ports.Store. Nothing new performs or reads an effect in Tier 1/2. The change also removes an existing violation: the CLI used to write backups directly through JsonFileStore.create, and the 'open Lending.Host.Persistence' line is now gone.",
            "score": 2
          },
          "ARC-REV-03": {
            "evidence": [
              {
                "file": "src/Lending.Application/Views.fs",
                "line": 325,
                "quote": "let summary (library: Library) : LibrarySummaryView ="
              },
              {
                "file": "src/Lending.Transition/Accounts.fs",
                "line": 22,
                "quote": "|> List.sumBy (fun memberId -> owed memberId library)"
              }
            ],
            "rationale": "Each fact has one definition. A member's balance reuses the existing Accounts.owed and is not restated. The library summary is defined once in Views.summary and shared by backup, restore and backup-info. The 'no backup at' refusal lives only in the private fromBackup helper, which both restore and backupInfo use.",
            "score": 2
          }
        },
        "2": {
          "ARC-REV-01": {
            "evidence": [
              {
                "file": "src/Lending.Transition/Accounts.fs",
                "line": 36,
                "quote": "do! ensure (not (library.Members.ContainsKey memberId)) (DuplicateMember memberId)"
              },
              {
                "file": "src/Lending.Application/UseCases.fs",
                "line": 203,
                "quote": "Accounts.restoreMember backup (MemberId memberId) library"
              }
            ],
            "rationale": "All the rules for restoring one member are decided in Tier 2 Accounts.restoreMember: the member must be in the backup, the member must not already exist, only that member's fines and payments come across, and loans, holds and reminders stay behind. The Tier 3 use case only loads the backup through the port and commits the result. Views and the CLI only project and render it.",
            "score": 2
          },
          "ARC-REV-02": {
            "evidence": [
              {
                "file": "src/Lending.Application/UseCases.fs",
                "line": 200,
                "quote": "fromBackup ports path"
              }
            ],
            "rationale": "No new effect is added. The backup is read through the existing Archive port (via fromBackup) and the state is saved through the existing commit/Store path. The Tier 2 function is pure: it takes two Library values and returns a Result. The CLI calls only the Tier 3 use case.",
            "score": 2
          },
          "ARC-REV-03": {
            "evidence": [
              {
                "file": "src/Lending.Transition/Accounts.fs",
                "line": 37,
                "quote": "let fines = finesOf memberId backup"
              }
            ],
            "rationale": "The change uses the existing definitions finesOf, paymentsOf and the DuplicateMember error, and the existing fromBackup refusal for a missing backup. It introduces no new limit, rate or date rule. The duplicate-member guard sits in Tier 2 and reports through the shared DuplicateMember error. Whether it repeats a guard elsewhere in Tier 2 can't be checked from the patch alone, and either way it stays in one tier and agrees with the existing error.",
            "score": 2
          }
